// only authored content this session is the wooden-furniture tree from Bible §A.5.4. An industry
// with no PRODUCT_CATALOG entry (Hospitality, currently) is completely unaffected — every
// function below returns neutral/empty results when `industry.productCatalog` is absent.
//
// STUBBED THIS SESSION, per the locked build order — these are honest placeholders, not the
// real systems, and are called out at each use site:
//   - Equipment: no Equipment entities with condition/precision exist yet (build order item 2).
//     Stood in for by COMPLETED PROJECT TAGS — "do you have a completed Tooling project" instead
//     of "do you own a CNC machine at 80% condition". The check is written as one function
//     (companyResourceProfile's equipment loop) so swapping in real Equipment later touches one
//     place.
//   - Suppliers: no supplier entities exist yet (build order item 3). Material adjacency is a
//     static tag comparison against materials used by products you've already produced, instead
//     of a real supplier-relationship check.
//   - Named employees / skills: no employee entities exist yet (build order item 4). Skill
//     adjacency is a static tag comparison against skills "learned" by having produced a product
//     that required them, instead of a real workforce skill check.
//
// capacityDemand resolution (Bible §0.2, DECIDED): capacity and demand remain exactly what they
// were — draft.capacity/draft.demand, the existing slow accumulator fed by generic Tooling/Line/
// Plant projects, with demand's existing decay/regrowth untouched. Products ADD a second,
// PURELY DERIVED term on top, recomputed fresh every month from live product state rather than
// accumulated — see productCapacityContribution/productDemandContribution. Nothing about the
// existing formula changes; this is composition, not replacement, which is the honest scope for
// "Products alone, equipment stubbed."

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- concurrent product slots
// Locked counts: 1 / 1 / 1 / 2 / 5 / 5. The 2->5 jump at Expansion is deliberate — Expansion is
// where the company stops being a manufacturer and becomes a portfolio.
