// ============================== BUSINESS MODEL LAYER ==============================
// The missing layer in Simulation Engine -> Industry -> [BUSINESS MODEL] -> Company -> Products.
//
// Three axes, three options each = 27 distinct strategic paths. They are committed at STAGGERED
// points in the run rather than all at once, so each is a real fork made with the information
// available at that moment, and the combination is discovered rather than picked from a menu at
// month 1 (the same reasoning that makes Founder Philosophy accumulate instead of being chosen).
//
// Commitments are PERMANENT, with a deliberately costly re-tool -- that's the locked decision.
// A commitment you regret is a story; a commitment you can freely swap is a settings screen.
//
// Effects are aggregated by activeModelEffects() exactly like activeTermEffects() does for
// funding terms, so no call site needs to know which commitments exist or how they stack. Both
// aggregators feed the same engine reads.
//
// Industry-agnostic on purpose: these are business-model questions, not industry mechanics. A
// restaurant group and a hardware company both genuinely face premium-vs-volume, build-vs-buy,
// and deepen-vs-broaden. Industries supply flavor text, not different axes.
